course: dictionary
lesson: 8361
title: Rotten: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Context, the words around the word, tells you which meaning fits. «Rotten eggs smell because bacteria break down proteins with sulphur in them» is about food that has gone bad, which is the first meaning.
explain: The meaning can change with the sentence. «I feel rotten» is not about food at all. It means feeling ill or unhappy. To check, put the meaning into the sentence: «I feel gone bad» does not make sense, so this must be the feeling meaning.
explain: Informal phrases change the meaning again. «Rotten luck» and «rotten weather» mean very bad or unpleasant. «Spoiled rotten» means someone was given too much and allowed everything. When a word appears in a new phrase, look at the words next to it.
fact: Rotten means gone bad, soft and smelly because of decay, like a rotten egg or rotten wood.
fact: Rotten can also mean very bad or unfair, as in rotten weather or a rotten trick.
fact: Rotten eggs smell because of a gas called hydrogen sulphide, which your nose can sense even in tiny amounts.
fact: Never eat food that looks, smells or tastes rotten, because it can make you ill.
fact: «Rotten apple» means one bad person in a group, and «rotten to the core» means dishonest all the way through.
exercise: «The apples were rotten, soft and brown inside.» What does rotten mean here? | Full of juice | Very old and ancient | *Gone bad and soft from decay | Very clean and shiny
exercise: Sam says, «I feel rotten today.» What does rotten mean here? | *Feeling ill or unhappy | Very fast | Covered in mud | A rotten egg in the fridge
exercise: Which phrase means one bad person in a group? | Rotten wood | *Rotten apple | Spoiled rotten | Rotten weather
test: «The rotten floorboard snapped under his foot.» Why is this dangerous? | The wood is very old and valuable | The wood is very clean | The wood smells of flowers | *The wood has decayed and is weak, so it can break
test: «It was rotten luck that the match was rained off.» What does rotten mean here? | Morally wrong | Given too much and spoiled | Gone bad from decay | *Very bad or unlucky
exam: Which sentence uses rotten to mean morally bad or dishonest? | *He was rotten to the core and cheated his friends | The old shed wood was rotten | The rotten egg stank in the bin | I feel rotten after the flu
